f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-10418" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}+8x+50y=129?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}+8x+50y & =129 \\\\ {x}^{2}+8x-5{y}^{2}+50y & =129 \\\\ {x}^{2}+8x-5[{y}^{2}-10y] & =129 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-16-5[(y-5)^{2}-25] & =129 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-16-5(y-5)^{2}+125 & =129 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-5(y-5)^{2} & =129+16-125 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}-5(y-5)^{2} & =20 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{20}-\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(-4,5).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-10418/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223e29c9-1bb5-51ee-9ec8-4d5c15363951"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10418"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78868/selection/8e6d20837836789dc7c71bf8fec566368831f74856656629274ba9d8d5d13e90" :answer/id #uuid "ae6df21f-943c-5bda-a647-56b849766d9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,9)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78868/selection/a2955f88f577e14b32ef8fabcc4bb70d4cd613455948b707cb3b55e13633d49b" :answer/id #uuid "6364d58e-2fd4-5f1f-877f-5b3230936160" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-4,7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78868/selection/d285ca37b852eea96f0f37710dc752c8379a3a2530a2ec387688a1a562b692cb" :answer/id #uuid "82ea2dc5-4aed-5797-8435-8c74b31f1e50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(9,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78868/selection/7daa24b81b950dafa8b7de5665a72f376bf2db54ea26beb16271955983287ae5" :answer/id #uuid "7318ed52-b5d6-52a1-a771-333d18578307" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(7,-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78868/selection/9afab023b17b6f95c090e51cac903393b0ad566ba54d7a560e6057a863955174" :answer/id #uuid "3e9e4df3-52af-5a57-9f44-011e417573b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,-7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78868/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f6b5fcd-1080-5de0-9c6e-99bbcb2f126d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78868/selection/a2955f88f577e14b32ef8fabcc4bb70d4cd613455948b707cb3b55e13633d49b" :answer-field/choices ["q-78868/selection/8e6d20837836789dc7c71bf8fec566368831f74856656629274ba9d8d5d13e90" "q-78868/selection/a2955f88f577e14b32ef8fabcc4bb70d4cd613455948b707cb3b55e13633d49b" "q-78868/selection/d285ca37b852eea96f0f37710dc752c8379a3a2530a2ec387688a1a562b692cb" "q-78868/selection/7daa24b81b950dafa8b7de5665a72f376bf2db54ea26beb16271955983287ae5" "q-78868/selection/9afab023b17b6f95c090e51cac903393b0ad566ba54d7a560e6057a863955174"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78868" :question/id #uuid "b2096e13-b432-5188-9b2a-286612b8e650" :question/math-academy-id "q-78868" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-7)^{2}}{9}-(x+4)^{2}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-7)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x-(-4))^{2}}{1}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=-4$ and $k=7.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(-4,7).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-78868/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdab0134-e416-51cf-89fa-73ad4a2c2eb9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78868"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-116113/selection/7a63746fb154abad8b03f812bbe07834b58e3ebbe52640c382bc0d9cd40b4132" :answer/id #uui