1bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "a8328a37-837b-5c78-8ad6-1ccb44c7b86c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328394/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "17106630-b05c-5222-886f-88b96dde7f23" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328394/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-328394/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328394/field-2/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "09ffd12b-b5c0-5d57-84c7-c1a648a1ef33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328394/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "77403b5d-1d0e-5bfc-ba96-5fe72a8010e3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328394/field-2/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-328394/field-2/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328394" :question/id #uuid "57c8250e-40fd-51ca-8080-031a88dc2b94" :question/math-academy-id "q-328394" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $9{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+36y+10x=25$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+36y+10x & =25 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+36y-{x}^{2}+10x & =25 \\\\ 9[{y}^{2}+4y]-[{x}^{2}-10x] & =25 \\\\ 9[(y+2)^{2}-4]-[(x-5)^{2}-25] & =25 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-36-(x-5)^{2}+25 & =25 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-(x-5)^{2} & =25+36-25 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-(x-5)^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{36} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(\\,5,-2\\,).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-328394/field-1" "q-328394/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328394"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
